1️⃣ Functional Overview — What the application does

Your module, ImportCustomersService, is part of a customer import and synchronization system that integrates:
	•	an internal BLM (Batch Loader Manager),
	•	a CRM system (like Salesforce),
	•	and external systems (CLS / ODS, etc.).

👉 Main Goal:

Take a batch file containing a list of customers or prospects,
and for each row, create or update the corresponding customer records in the CRM and other systems.

⸻

⚙️ Functional Flow

1. Read the batch

Each batch (LoaderBatch) has:
	•	a unique ID,
	•	a country (GB, FR, etc.),
	•	a file name,
	•	a type (CONTACTS, CUSTOMERS, etc.),
	•	the total number of contacts.

The service loops through all rows (each one is a CustomerPayload).

⸻

2. Validate each customer

Each row (CustomerPayload) contains:
	•	crmData → CRM details (title, name, gender, country, etc.)
	•	clsData → technical data
	•	errorMessage → optional (if not null, the record is invalid)

➡️ If a record has an errorMessage, it’s skipped and a step event is recorded with status KO (failure).

⸻

3. Generate technical IDs

For valid rows:
	•	A rowReference (unique per line) is created using ReferenceIdFactory.
	•	A reconciliationId is built (to link batch and CRM records).
	•	The CrmClsCustomerData model is created (the unified data model for CRM + CLS).

⸻

4. CRM interaction

Depending on the customer’s state:
	•	isCreateRole() → create a role in CRM
	•	isUpdateRole() → update an existing role
	•	isCrmUpdate() → update the customer in CRM
	•	otherwise → create a new CRM customer

Each action interacts with SPI ports (interfaces for external systems):
	•	crmCustomerProviderSpi → CRM API (create/update)
	•	crmClsCustomerDataRepositorySpi → internal DB
	•	recordStepEventRepositorySpi → audit logs

⸻

5. Log step events

After each operation, a RecordStepEvent is saved:
	•	batchId
	•	rowNumber
	•	reconciliationId
	•	stepName (e.g., SF_CREATE, SF_UPDATE)
	•	stepStatus (OK or KO)
	•	message
	•	timestamp

Example:

✅ “Customer #4 successfully created in CRM”
❌ “Customer #2 failed: invalid country code”

⸻

6. Update the batch

When all rows are processed:
	•	updateBatchStatus() is called
	•	The batch is marked as IMPORTED
	•	The endDate is updated to the current time

⸻

🔧 2️⃣ Technical Overview — How the application is built

🏗️ Architecture: Hexagonal (Ports & Adapters)
	•	Domain layer → entities like CustomerPayload, CrmClsCustomerData, LoaderBatch, RecordStepEvent
	•	Application layer → ImportCustomersService (business logic)
	•	Ports (SPI) → interfaces for external dependencies
	•	Adapters → actual implementations (e.g., CRM REST client, DB repository)
